# Cloudflare Workers static-assets header rules. The hashed JS/CSS bundles
# already have unique filenames per build (content-addressed), so they're
# safe to cache forever -- but the top-level HTML pages (/, /app,
# /architecture, etc.) share the same URL across deploys, so without an
# explicit rule an edge cache or a visitor's browser can keep serving an
# old build's HTML after a new one ships.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
